---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import {
  BROWSER_STORAGE,
  DATA_CATEGORIES,
  ESSENTIAL_COOKIES,
  PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE,
  RETENTION_ROWS,
  THIRD_PARTIES,
} from "../data/privacy";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — NovaGuard"
  description="What NovaGuard processes, why it is needed, how long it is kept, and the essential storage used by the website."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] text-ink-muted uppercase">
      Effective {PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE}
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      This policy covers the NovaGuard Discord bot, dashboard and website operated by VIK &amp;
      CloudMedia. It explains what data is processed, why it is needed, where it goes and how long
      it remains.
    </p>

    <aside class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-line bg-card p-5" aria-label="Privacy summary">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">The short version</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        NovaGuard has no advertising, does not sell personal data and currently uses no
        third-party analytics. The website sets only security and sign-in cookies required to
        provide the requested service, so there is no non-essential cookie choice to accept.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section id="your-choices" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-8 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">01 · Data inventory</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Information NovaGuard processes</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[42rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-bg-subtle text-ink">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Category</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">What it includes</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Why it is used</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
            {
              DATA_CATEGORIES.map((row) => (
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-medium text-ink">{row.name}</th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.data}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.use}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">02 · Cookies</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Essential cookies only</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        These cookies are first-party, are not used for advertising or cross-site tracking, and
        are sent with <code>HttpOnly</code> and <code>SameSite</code> protections. Production cookies
        are sent over HTTPS. Blocking them prevents the related sign-in, access or preview flow
        from working.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[42rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-bg-subtle text-ink">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Cookie</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Used for</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Purpose</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Lifetime</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
            {
              ESSENTIAL_COOKIES.map((row) => (
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-mono font-normal text-ink">{row.name}</th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-ink-muted">{row.when}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.purpose}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-ink-muted">{row.lifetime}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-display mt-9 text-xl">Browser storage</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The website also stores two small first-party preferences in the browser. Neither contains
        a Discord identity, and neither is sent with web requests.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-5 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          BROWSER_STORAGE.map((row) => (
            <div class="grid gap-2 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <dt>
                <code class="text-sm text-ink">{row.name}</code>
                <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-ink-faint">{row.lifetime}</span>
              </dt>
              <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.purpose}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">03 · Retention</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">How long data is kept</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          RETENTION_ROWS.map((row) => (
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] sm:gap-8">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{row.data}</dt>
              <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.period}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        A backup can retain an item until that backup reaches its own deletion window. Legal or
        security obligations may require a limited record to be kept longer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">04 · Processors</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Third-party services</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Data is shared only to operate NovaGuard or an optional integration selected by the server
        operator. Each provider handles the data it receives under its own policy.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          THIRD_PARTIES.map((provider) => (
            <li class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <a
                href={provider.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
                class="font-medium text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-primary"
              >
                {provider.name}
              </a>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{provider.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">05 · Your choices</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Access, export and deletion</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          A server administrator can export that server's stored settings, levels, economy and
          voice records with <code>/config export</code>. Logging out revokes the active Discord
          OAuth token and removes the dashboard session.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may also have rights to access, correct, delete,
          restrict or object to processing of personal data. Start a request using the contact
          details on the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/VIK-DD/NovaGuard"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
          >NovaGuard repository</a
          >. Do not post personal data in a public issue; arrange a private channel with the
          operator first. Include the relevant Discord user ID or server ID only after that, and
          never send a password, bot token or OAuth token. Identity or server authority may need to
          be verified before a request is completed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">06 · Security and changes</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Safeguards</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Dashboard OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest, session identifiers are hashed in the
        database, changes are access-controlled and audited, and production traffic uses HTTPS.
        No transmission or storage method is completely secure. Material policy changes will be
        published here with a new effective date.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
